From: Tove Petersson <tovep@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:18:05 -0700
Subject: [mac] Reject overlapping Open() calls in NativeScreenCapturePickerMac

NativeScreenCapturePickerMac is a browser-wide singleton. When Open()
is invoked while a system picker interaction is already in progress,
it previously overwrote the active callbacks and incremented the active
source ID without notifying the earlier requester. If the user then
selected a window or screen, the capture stream would be misdelivered
to the second requester instead of the original tab.

This CL ensures that Open() immediately rejects overlapping requests
via error_callback if picker_callback_ is already active. In addition,
closing the active picker session resets any pending callbacks so
subsequent requests can be served.

Bug: 518239793
Change-Id: I2eca753d630d1552a9a92a9abb82a8edac445145
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8430557
Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron <kron@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Tove Petersson <tovep@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1721813}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
This branch predates the picker-deactivation refactor (upstream 8324087):
OnPickerObserverCancelled()/OnPickerObserverEncounteredError() did not yet
clear the sibling callbacks and there is no MaybeDeactivatePicker()
(Close() deactivates the picker itself). The fix relies on picker_callback_
being cleared once the in-flight request ends, so those two handlers now
reset the other two callbacks before running their own, exactly as in the
upstream pre-image; MaybeDeactivatePicker() calls are not carried. The
Open() rejection, the null-callback guards and the Close() reset are
unchanged. native_screen_capture_picker_mac_unittest.mm is not carried
(test helper signatures differ on this branch).

